  "reply_text": "Found **one merge-blocking bug**:\n\n**[P1] `topTags` mutates the input, breaking the sidebar’s “recent” strip** — `src/tags.js:10`  \n`tags.sort(...)` sorts the caller’s array in place. Since `sidebar()` builds the cloud before taking `tags.slice(0, 5)` (`src/render.js:4–5`), “recent” shows the most popular tags instead of the first tags in the supplied order. This also violates the documented non-mutation contract.\n\nReproduced with input `[newest:1, popular:9, middle:4]`: “recent” becomes `[popular, middle, newest]`, and the original array is reordered.\n\n**Suggested fix:** sort a copy in `topTags`. Add regression tests asserting that the input remains unchanged and that `sidebar().recent` preserves supplied order.\n\nAll 4 existing tests pass, but none cover this behavior. No files changed.",
